Ants are the single biggest killer of players on hosts
that keep records.  There are certain types of monsters
that are strong out of depth and ants are the first one
many players hit.  While any one of them is at depth,
ants are fast so you have very little time to handle them
once you see them and they come in groups.

There are other out of depth monster types at various
levels of the dungeon but ants are the one that cause
the most deaths.  Learnig to deal with ants is a major
skill task of the early game - I take early game to mean
until the mines and sokoban are completed.

The biggest factor when facing ants is to keep from
getting surrounded as you've seen.  No matter what you
are doing when you see the first ant, head for the nearest
corridor.  No monster is important enough to combat that
it is worth dying surrounded by ants just to kill that one
monster.  Survive a group of ants and you can always
mop up that monster aferwards.  Also always be very
ready to rush back up the stairs when it look like you
might get in trouble.  Start running before you're down
to half of your hit points and you're likely to survive and
heal.


